{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-4-6","id":"msg_vrtx_01Pw9HLF1AvMgiZQ6MZbE3jj","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Done. Here's what was written for **Q14: Bias/fairness tradeoffs — example?**\n\n---\n\n**Key content in `05-014-biasfairness-tradeoffs-example.md`:**\n\n- **Concept:** Fairness is a family of competing, mathematically incompatible definitions — not a single metric. The three main ones are demographic parity, equalized odds, and calibration.\n\n- **Impossibility theorem:** Chouldechova 2017 — when base rates differ between groups, you cannot simultaneously achieve equalized odds AND calibration. You must choose.\n\n- **Mechanism:** Three intervention levers:\n  1. **Threshold adjustment** (post-processing, fastest) — different cutoffs per group to equalize TPR/FPR\n  2. **Re-weighting / re-sampling** (in-processing, more durable)\n  3. **Adversarial debiasing** (in-processing, most expensive, closes gap at representation level)\n\n- **Concrete example:** Resume screening classifier with 78% overall accuracy but a 23-point recall gap between male/female candidates — surfaced via Fairlearn, fixed with threshold adjustment (closed to 4pts), then re-weighting in next training cycle. Metric targets: demographic parity gap ≤0.05, subgroup recall/FPR tracked weekly in Grafana.\n\n- **Production angle:** Fairness must be a CI gate (subgroup recall in deployment pipeline), not a one-time audit. Fairness regressions between model versions are as serious as accuracy regressions.\n\n- **Pitfalls called out:** Conflating \"equal accuracy per group\" with fairness; treating fairness as a one-time audit; claiming all definitions can be satisfied simultaneously."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":327,"cache_read_input_tokens":67814,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":327,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":1},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"33d183c6-db65-4b02-962d-4baa14f50c3a","uuid":"5f54607f-35fc-4ea4-a9e4-532d880371d7"}
